<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index fell five points to 1,513.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index fell five points to 1,513.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates fell to 1,513 today from 1,518 on March 26, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p>  Route Index     Rate    Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1527    13.864	  1525    13.844</p>
<p>   1a   1533 11607.000	  1544 11694.000</p>
<p>   2    1813    25.900	  1812    25.881</p>
<p>   2a   1876 15386.000	  1878 15400.000</p>
<p>   3    1750    16.143	  1754    16.181</p>
<p>   3a   1629 12857.000	  1642 12963.000</p>
<p>   6    1235    12.743	  1238    12.769</p>
<p>   7    1144     5.571	  1148     5.588</p>
<p>   8     925    10.171	   928    10.206</p>
<p>   9    1032  9029.000	  1043  9119.000</p>
<p>  10    1092     5.514	  1093     5.519</p>
